      "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe scheduler receives logprob rows from tensor and host-list backends. Unconditionally calling `.tolist()` on host-list rows raises `AttributeError` during decode or response construction.\n\n## Modifications\n\nNormalize logprob value/index rows only when they are tensors. Preserve already materialized Python lists, including targeted token-id rows, in the CPU move and decode paths. Add a regression that exercises host-list decode normalization.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nAt exact HEAD `60bd318b3be0ba1cb18192bdae92c64ba2893c32`, `test/registered/unit/layers/test_logprob_chunk_stitching.py` passes **5 tests** (17 warnings, 14.78 seconds) via pytest in a disposable ARM64 container with no GPU devices exposed. Direct CI-style `python test/registered/unit/layers/test_logprob_chunk_stitching.py -f` also passes all 5 tests.\n\nThe new regression against pinned pre-fix source `7ff3a112846a3fcc12a27bba09d644885a226e4d` fails as expected with `AttributeError: 'list' object has no attribute 'tolist'` at `batch_result_processor.py:1125`, demonstrating sensitivity to the original fault. The container uses Torch 2.13.0+cu130, Transformers 5.12.1 and pytest 9.1.1; public source is mounted read-only.\n\nThe coverage run passes all 5 tests. Changed production-line coverage against pinned base `7ff3a112846a3fcc12a27bba09d644885a226e4d` is **100% (2/2 lines)**; `diff-cover --fail-under=60` exits 0. Coverage tools were installed only in the disposable validation container. This patch is independent of quantization and does not claim to fix model repetition behavior.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo model throughput benchmark was run. The change preserves already materialized host lists and adds tensor type checks to response conversion; no GPU kernels or model numerics change.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] `pre-commit run --all-files` passes at exact HEAD: all 30 applicable hooks, including Rust formatting and Clippy; no tracked files changed.\n- [x] Add registered CPU regression coverage and verify direct CLI execution and pre-fix failure.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style guidance.\n- [x] Changed production-line coverage is 100%, exceeding the registered unit-test guide's 60% threshold.\n\nThank you for reviewing. An authorized maintainer's `run-ci` label and required reviews are still pending.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38449894914](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38449894914)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38449894814](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38449894814)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38449894395](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38449894395)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
